{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Avimelech said.</b> Since the first verse is a rebuke and an acceptance, whereas this utterance is a question to know his reason — for surely he did not intend to do harm, but his reason was hidden within him — therefore Scripture dedicated a separate utterance to ask him: ״מָה רָאִיתָ״ and so on."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:28.584787122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}